ai_response:
Based on the retrieved context, under Section 4(1)(b) of the RTI Act, the Department of Administrative Reforms and Public Grievances (DARPG) is required to publish proactively on its website:

"Organisational chart;
Rules, regulations, instructions, manuals and records, held by or under the control of the public authority; 
A statement of the boards, councils, committees and other bodies constituted as its part or for advising it;
Terms and conditions of the constitution of each such board, council, committee and other body; Powers and duties of its officers and employees;
Procedure followed in the decision making process, including channels of supervision and accountability;
The details of facilities available to citizens for obtaining information, including the working hours of a library or reading room, if maintained by it;
Subsidies, grants and concessions received by it from the Government and amounts of subsidies, grants and concessions given by it to other persons."

(Section 4(1)(b), Right to Information Act, 2005)

Source: RTI Act, 2005 (India)
